{"loin":{"id":"9146c852-b88c-418e-ae2a-92be96585672","word":"loin","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"part of the body","tags":["masculine"],"word":"lombo"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"cut of meat","tags":["masculine"],"word":"lombo"}],"pos":"noun","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"Holonym: side","id":"53257dc0-b812-4c72-8577-9b2b9c3d2e32"}],"senseid":["en:anatomy"],"links":[["body","body"],["human","human"],["quadruped","quadruped"],["backbone","backbone"],["rib","rib"],["hip","hip"]],"synonyms":[{"word":"lend"},{"word":"lumbus"}],"coordinate_terms":[{"word":"flank"}],"glosses":["The part of the body (of humans and quadrupeds) at each side of the backbone, between the ribs and hips."],"id":"9e7f8dfb-1649-4551-b9ed-898e651890a4"},{"links":[["cut","cut"],["meat","meat"],["animal","animal"]],"glosses":["Any of several cuts of meat taken from this part of an animal."],"id":"f4d10269-89ea-4e0f-8513-a7be36f923d7"}],"related":[{"word":"lumbago"},{"word":"lumbar"}],"synonyms":[]},"loins":{"id":"a1533791-2fb5-42ef-b291-388e02db558d","word":"loins","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"the lower abdomen, groin and genitalia","word":"virilhas"}],"pos":"noun","tags":null,"senses":[{"topics":["biblical","lifestyle","religion"],"categories":["English euphemisms","en:Bible"],"links":[["biblical","Bible"],["pubic region","pubic region"]],"raw_glosses":["(biblical, euphemistic) The pubic region."],"glosses":["The pubic region."],"tags":["euphemistic","plural","plural-only"],"id":"98398000-657c-47c8-8c79-8acaf3e39730"},{"examples":[{"text":"Neuertheleſſe, thou ſhalt not build the houſe, but thy ſonne that ſhall come foorth out of thy loynes, hee ſhall build the house vnto my Name.","ref":"1611, The Holy Bible, […] (King James Version), London: […] Robert Barker, […], →OCLC, 1 Kings 8:19, column 1:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[95,101]],"id":"5daa483e-1d46-416f-8bdd-8c34c5cc8468"}],"topics":["biblical","lifestyle","religion"],"categories":["English euphemisms","English terms with quotations","en:Bible"],"links":[["biblical","Bible"],["pubic region","pubic region"],["reproductive","reproductive"],["organ","organ"]],"raw_glosses":["(biblical, euphemistic) The pubic region.","The reproductive organs."],"glosses":["The pubic region.","The reproductive organs."],"tags":["euphemistic","plural","plural-only"],"id":"c58dcb91-253d-49e8-879f-ed2780d05e4e"}],"related":[{"word":"lumb-"},{"word":"lumbo-"},{"word":"lumbago"},{"word":"lumbar"},{"word":"lumbosacral"}],"synonyms":[]},"loiter":{"id":"d5f0547d-bce2-4f55-aa19-3f9f8b7d4bbf","word":"loiter","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"to stand about without any aim or purpose","word":"vadiar"}],"pos":"verb","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"For some reason, they discourage loitering outside the store, but encourage it inside.","bold_text_offsets":[[33,42]],"type":"example","id":"2885701b-d25a-4d47-824c-936f9c7a07ec"}],"links":[["idly","idly"]],"synonyms":[{"word":"lepak","tags":["Malaysia","Singapore"]},{"word":"linger"},{"word":"hang around"}],"glosses":["To stand about without any aim or purpose; to stand about idly."],"categories":["English terms with usage examples"],"id":"fe25fe60-6969-47d0-8549-e0c31e88dca5"},{"examples":[{"text":"With weary steps I loiter on,\n⁠Tho’ always under alter’d skies\n⁠The purple from the distance dies,\nMy prospect and horizon gone.","ref":"1850, [Alfred, Lord Tennyson], “Canto XXXVIII”, in In Memoriam, London: Edward Moxon, […], →OCLC, page 59:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[19,25]],"id":"a8219e0d-673f-453b-bbf8-7f366d800759"}],"categories":["English terms with archaic senses","English terms with quotations"],"links":[["stroll","stroll"],["ramble","ramble"],["wander","wander"]],"raw_glosses":["(archaic) To stroll about without any aim or purpose, to ramble, to wander."],"glosses":["To stroll about without any aim or purpose, to ramble, to wander."],"tags":["archaic"],"id":"05630a28-e43d-43f4-ba92-2084c11171cb"},{"examples":[{"text":"The dancing, which had been suspended, now recommenced with additional animation, and De Candale claimed Francesca's hand; but the rooms were crowded, and they stood for some time loitering on one of the terraces.","ref":"1834, L[etitia] E[lizabeth] L[andon], chapter V, in Francesca Carrara. […], volume II, London: Richard Bentley, […], (successor to Henry Colburn), →OCLC, page 47:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[180,189]],"id":"fe8250a0-825f-4bf7-b720-c46e6c0894ac"},{"text":"For on what does the whole vast and varied membership of the craft rest? It rests, of course, on the little boys whom you see any day loitering about on the far end of station platforms in every part of the British Isles, each one with his grubby notebook and blunt pencil, and his list of all the engines on the railway system, collecting their numbers and names in the vain hope that one day he will have collected them all.","ref":"1948 September and October, Canon Roger Lloyd, “The Art and Mystery of the Railway”, in Railway Magazine, page 331:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[134,143]],"id":"654e41eb-a5bd-4db0-a197-fa9633e4f74a"},{"text":"[Sergio] Agüero, as usual, was loitering with intent and swung his left foot at the ball. The shot was going wide but [David] Silva was there to apply the decisive touch inside the six-yard area.","ref":"2015 January 31, Daniel Taylor, “David Silva seizes point for Manchester City as Chelsea are checked”, in The Guardian, London, archived from the original on 08 Mar 2017:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[31,40]],"id":"81a5331a-627f-4b63-b42d-fb20fb67bb6e"},{"text":"Using the transect method, the counter had to maintain a general progress along the transect and was not able to loiter at one spot for too long.","ref":"2019, Li Huang, James Lambert, “Another Arrow for the Quiver: A New Methodology for Multilingual Researchers”, in Journal of Multilingual and Multicultural Development, →DOI, page 4:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[113,119]],"id":"ed59ad10-4fff-4fa2-a439-d254e4d5c805"}],"categories":["English terms with quotations"],"glosses":["To remain at a certain place instead of moving on."],"id":"341c22a5-f6ef-4280-a032-bc313562b200"},{"topics":["aeronautics","aerospace","aviation","business","engineering","government","military","natural-sciences","physical-sciences","politics","war"],"categories":["en:Aviation","en:Military"],"links":[["military","military"],["aviation","aviation"]],"raw_glosses":["(military, aviation) For an aircraft to remain in the air near a target."],"glosses":["For an aircraft to remain in the air near a target."],"id":"e46facc3-cc0d-44b2-86ef-6cbb759f06b9"}],"related":[{"word":"build castles in the air","source":"Thesaurus:loiter"},{"word":"time bandit","source":"Thesaurus:loiter"},{"word":"time burglar","source":"Thesaurus:loiter"},{"word":"time thief","source":"Thesaurus:loiter"},{"word":"idler","source":"Thesaurus:loiter"},{"word":"lazy","source":"Thesaurus:loiter"},{"word":"shirk","source":"Thesaurus:loiter"}],"synonyms":[{"word":"arse about","source":"Thesaurus:loiter"},{"word":"arse around","source":"Thesaurus:loiter"},{"word":"bludge","source":"Thesaurus:loiter","tags":["Australia","New-Zealand","slang"]},{"word":"bum around","source":"Thesaurus:loiter"},{"word":"cabbage","source":"Thesaurus:loiter","tags":["slang"]},{"word":"clown around","source":"Thesaurus:loiter"},{"word":"dally","source":"Thesaurus:loiter"},{"word":"dawdle","source":"Thesaurus:loiter"},{"word":"dick about","source":"Thesaurus:loiter"},{"word":"dick around","source":"Thesaurus:loiter"},{"word":"diddle","source":"Thesaurus:loiter"},{"word":"dilly-dally","source":"Thesaurus:loiter"},{"word":"dretch","source":"Thesaurus:loiter","tags":["Scotland"]},{"word":"drumble","source":"Thesaurus:loiter","tags":["obsolete"]},{"word":"faff","source":"Thesaurus:loiter"},{"word":"faff about","source":"Thesaurus:loiter"},{"word":"faff around","source":"Thesaurus:loiter"},{"word":"fanny about","source":"Thesaurus:loiter"},{"word":"fanny around","source":"Thesaurus:loiter"},{"word":"fart about","source":"Thesaurus:loiter"},{"word":"fart around","source":"Thesaurus:loiter"},{"word":"fiddle about","source":"Thesaurus:loiter"},{"word":"fiddle around","source":"Thesaurus:loiter"},{"word":"fool about","source":"Thesaurus:loiter"},{"word":"fool around","source":"Thesaurus:loiter"},{"word":"footle","source":"Thesaurus:loiter"},{"word":"forslow","source":"Thesaurus:loiter"},{"word":"goof around","source":"Thesaurus:loiter"},{"word":"goof off","source":"Thesaurus:loiter"},{"word":"hang about","source":"Thesaurus:loiter"},{"word":"hang around","source":"Thesaurus:loiter"},{"word":"hang out","source":"Thesaurus:loiter"},{"word":"horse around","source":"Thesaurus:loiter"},{"word":"idle","source":"Thesaurus:loiter"},{"word":"jerk off","source":"Thesaurus:loiter","tags":["vulgar"]},{"word":"lallygag","source":"Thesaurus:loiter"},{"word":"lamp","source":"Thesaurus:loiter","tags":["slang"]},{"word":"laze","source":"Thesaurus:loiter"},{"word":"laze about","source":"Thesaurus:loiter"},{"word":"laze around","source":"Thesaurus:loiter"},{"word":"linger","source":"Thesaurus:loiter"},{"word":"loaf","source":"Thesaurus:loiter"},{"word":"loaf about","source":"Thesaurus:loiter"},{"word":"loaf around","source":"Thesaurus:loiter"},{"word":"loiter","source":"Thesaurus:loiter"},{"word":"lollop","source":"Thesaurus:loiter"},{"word":"lollygag","source":"Thesaurus:loiter"},{"word":"mess around","source":"Thesaurus:loiter"},{"word":"mill about","source":"Thesaurus:loiter"},{"word":"mill around","source":"Thesaurus:loiter"},{"word":"muck about","source":"Thesaurus:loiter"},{"word":"muck around","source":"Thesaurus:loiter"},{"word":"piddle","source":"Thesaurus:loiter"},{"word":"pingle","source":"Thesaurus:loiter","tags":["Britain","dialectal"]},{"word":"stand by","sou